SNI-Spoofing-Go
---------------
Source: https://github.com/aleskxyz/SNI-Spoofing-Go
Commit: f60734498c5dcdfd85705f4a682af5871d01895c (built unmodified)
License: GPL-3.0

Shipped as `libsnispoof.so` in `app/src/main/jniLibs/<abi>/`: a standalone executable the app runs
as a separate root process (`su -c`) and talks to only over a local TCP port and its command line.
It is not linked into the app. Built with
`GOOS=android CGO_ENABLED=1 go build -trimpath -buildmode=pie -ldflags="-s -w"` against the NDK
clang for each ABI, with 16 KB page alignment. The corresponding source is the commit above; the
full license text is in that repository's LICENSE file.

Hidden space sim
----------------
The easter egg in `ui/easteregg/` is an original implementation, written for this app, of the
game design of "Landroid" — the space exploration sim that has shipped as the Android platform
easter egg since Android 14 (`frameworks/base/packages/EasterEgg`, Apache-2.0). The flight-stick
control scheme, the Newtonian drift with a suspended-gravity launch window, the attitude-based
landing criterion, the autopilot's chase/approach/land strategies and the phosphor-console
telemetry are all taken from its design. No AOSP source is reproduced here.

