SlipNet
-------
Source: https://github.com/anonvector/SlipNet — anonvector

Versions before 3.0.9 included SlipNet's dnstt fork (AGPL-3.0), noizdns, and
vaydns-mobile in the core, including SlipNet's TCP transport. Since 3.0.9, the
core uses zeddns, which has the same features with its own code. These features
come from SlipNet: DNS over plain TCP, the fan-out and round-robin resolver
modes with spread count, the DNS pool, the global resolver override and
prevent-DNS-fallback settings, and the design and text of the DNS and SSH settings.

